name air-fishbed-guns
timeout 300

# THE CANNON HALF of the catalogue's fire control, and the row is deliberately one carrying NOTHING on
# its rails: `mig21` with no `set store` line at all. What that proves is the shape of the box —
# fc_dlz stays 0 for the whole run because there is no round to solve a launch zone FOR, while
# fc_gun_err_deg and the funnel gate are live from the first lock. A row's armament decides which of the
# fire control's products exists, and the file measures that instead of asserting it.
#
# WHY THIS ROW AND NOT `mig17`. The MiG-17 and the Su-7 are the two rows whose ONLY weapon is a cannon,
# and neither can aim one: they carry NO radar (SearchRangeM 0), the gun solution needs a RANGE, and the
# eye publishes an angular size and no range at all. That is booked as doc/modules/air/module.md A14 with
# the mechanism the fix needs (a gyro gunsight ranges on a DIALLED-IN wingspan). `mig21` is the shortest
# path to the same question with a ranging source on board — and its deck is one of the four `ACCEPTED`,
# so recipe step 8 has written its measured roll plant (a = 0.724278, K = 318.528 deg/s) and the tier
# gate lets it into the close-combat phase at all.
#
# THE CAST
#   fishbed  hostile `mig21`, T3, GSh-23L with 200 rounds, no missiles. Bounced from astern at 760 m,
#            because a catalogue deck's close-combat law cannot CLOSE: from 3 nm it took 76 s to reach
#            0.9 nm and then overshot (measured, A15). The bounce is the geometry in which the gun
#            question can be asked at all today, and the file says so rather than hiding it.
#   courier  friendly `an26`, a MOVER on a straight leg — one zone, `Structure` alone.
#
# MEASURED 2026-07-29:
#   t = 4.5 s   `pilot GUN_TRACK` rangeM 464, aimErrDeg 8.72, spanMr 15.4 against a funnel bottom of
#               11.27 mr — the funnel is the GSh-23L's own: 715 m/s x 0.888 s = 635 m far end [DERIVED]
#   t = 7.1 s   `gun TRIGGER` burstS 0.5, and again at t = 8.1 s
#   t = 7.7 .. 8.8 s   FOUR `gun HIT` lines, the last at 38 173 J/m^2 -> `damage SYSTEM structure
#               degraded` on the An-26
#   t = 11.4 s  `pilot GUN_BREAK` at 66 m
#
# READING RULE: the PRODUCT of this file is the four `gun HIT` lines and the `damage SYSTEM` line that
# follows them — a catalogue row employing its cannon through its own fire control. THE EXIT CODE IS NOT
# THE VERDICT HERE: the run currently ends `exit 2, CRASH` at t = 147.9 s, because after the pass the
# close-combat law flies the MiG-21 into the ground from 5 000 m without ever re-attacking, and its
# 2 000 ft floor does not hold it (impact at 424 m). That is doc/modules/air/module.md A15 — a
# BFM-on-a-raw-generated-deck defect with its own cause, measured here and not fixed here. A run with
# ZERO `gun TRIGGER` lines is the failure this file guards against.

unit fishbed
  team hostile
  module mig21
  spawn 46.90000 6.87000 5000 90.0 290
  set gear up
  set task bfm
  set brief_master_arm arm
  wp 46.90000 7.60000 5000 400

unit courier
  team friendly
  module an26
  spawn 46.90000 6.88000 5000 90.0 240
  wp 46.90000 7.90000 5000 240
  objective survive
